# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Volcanic
composer Claude
about    Black rock and rivers of lava: a horn in C Phrygian over a low pizzicato ostinato that keeps hammering, a tuba under a dark string pad and a bell clanging like an anvil once a bar. When something is near, the taiko drums and timpani take over; brass and the kit join the fight, and a choir, gong and thunder come for a guardian.
tempo    84
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.4

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead ostinato tuba pad anvil
# mood treasure: ostinato pad anvil wonder
# mood sense:    taiko_lo taiko_hi timpani tuba pad
# mood rise:     sense lead ostinato kick snare
# mood fight:    rise brass crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead -ostinato choir gong thunder

voice lead     horn      vol=0.65 pan=-0.1
voice ostinato pizz      vol=0.5  pan=0.3
voice tuba     tuba      vol=0.65 gate=0.9
voice pad      strings   vol=0.22 pan=-0.25 center=G3 att=0.5 rel=0.8
voice anvil    bell      vol=0.18 pan=0.4  rev=0.5
voice wonder   celesta   vol=0.38 pan=-0.35 rev=0.6
voice timpani  timpani   vol=0.55 pan=-0.1
voice taiko_lo tomlo     vol=0.6  pan=-0.25
voice taiko_hi tomhi     vol=0.45 pan=0.25
voice kick     kick      vol=0.55
voice snare    snare     vol=0.38 pan=0.1
voice brass    brass     vol=0.4  pan=-0.2 gate=0.8 center=G3
voice crash    crash     vol=0.22 pan=0.2
voice choir    choir     vol=0.32 center=C4 att=0.4 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong      vol=0.32 pan=-0.3
voice thunder  thunder   vol=0.2

# Cm Db Cm Bb | Ab Db Cm Cm: the motif with the flat second (C Db Eb G F)
